  "body": "##  AI Code Review Findings (Model: `gemini-3.5-flash`)\n\n###    [MEDIUM] Double-escaped backslashes in INJECTION_PATTERNS regex literals disable prompt injection detection\n**File:** `utils/jdValidator.ts` (Lines: 110-114)\n\nChanged Symbol: validateJobDescription\nAffected Caller: JDUploadStep / DeviceCheckWizard\nFailure Mode: The regex literals in `INJECTION_PATTERNS` use double-escaped backslashes (`/\\\\b.../`) instead of single backslashes (`/\\b.../`). In JavaScript RegExp literals, `\\\\b` matches a literal backslash character (`\\`) followed by `b` rather than a word boundary (`\\b`).\nUser Impact: Prompt injection inputs (such as \"ignore all previous instructions\" or \"system prompt\") will fail to trigger `isPromptInjection` and will bypass security validation.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\n```diff\n@@ -110,5 +110,5 @@\n const INJECTION_PATTERNS = [\n-  /\\\\bignore\\s+(all\\s+)?(previous|prior)\\s+instructions\\b/i,\n-  /\\\\bsystem\\s+prompt\\b/i,\n-  /\\\\bgive\\s+me\\s+(a\\s+)?(100|perfect|full)\\s+score\\b/i,\n+  /\\bignore\\s+(all\\s+)?(previous|prior)\\s+instructions\\b/i,\n+  /\\bsystem\\s+prompt\\b/i,\n+  /\\bgive\\s+me\\s+(a\\s+)?(100|perfect|full)\\s+score\\b/i,\n ];\n```\n\n---\n\n\n",
